  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets are finite?\n\n- $P({R,e})$\n- $P({x\\in R\u2223\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=0})$\n- $P({(-1)^{n}\u2223n\\in Z})$",
  "worked_solution": "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({R,e})={\u2205,\\,{R},\\,{e},\\,{R,e}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set II is infinite since the underlying set ${x\\in R\u2223\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=0}$  is infinite.\n\n- Set III is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n{(-1)^{n}\u2223n\\in Z}={-1,1},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP({(-1)^{n}\u2223n\\in Z})=P({-1,1})={\u2205,\\,{-1},\\,{1},\\,{-1,1}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
